---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="The Koy Pen — Daf Yomi Game: Chullin 80"
  description="Chullin 80: the koy is a hybrid of a wild deer and a domestic goat — and which parent is which decides everything. Sort six real rulings into the right pen, then meet five sages who can't agree what a koy even is."
>
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link
    rel="stylesheet"
    href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Frank+Ruhl+Libre:wght@400;700;900&display=swap"
  />

  <main class="min-h-screen bg-[#0c0a11] !text-[#eae3d2]">
    <!-- ============ Hero ============ -->
    <div class="border-b border-[#2b2438] bg-gradient-to-b from-[#191327]/80 to-transparent px-4 pt-10 pb-8 text-center">
      <p class="mb-3 text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.3em] !text-[#c08b3f]">
        <a href="/daf" class="hover:!text-[#dfa14e]">daf yomi arcade</a> · chullin 80 · 2026-07-18
      </p>
      <h1 class="frank text-4xl font-black tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">🧬 The Koy Pen</h1>
      <p class="frank mt-1 text-2xl !text-[#dfa14e]" dir="rtl" lang="he">שֶׂה וַאֲפִילּוּ מִקְצָת שֶׂה</p>
      <p class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-xl text-sm leading-relaxed !text-[#a19aad]">
        A koy is what happens when a wild deer and a domestic goat produce young. Half its blood is
        undomesticated, half is not — and the Rabbis rule that <em>"sheep"</em> in the Torah means
        <span class="frank !text-[#dfa14e]" dir="rtl" lang="he">שֶׂה וַאֲפִילּוּ מִקְצָת שֶׂה</span>,
        <em>even a partial sheep</em>, while Rabbi Eliezer disagrees (80a:1). Rav Pappa then shows the
        koy's laws only make sense once you ask <strong class="!text-[#eae3d2]">which parent was which</strong>.
        Two pens, two crosses, one riddle of paternity — sort the rulings, then meet the sages who
        never even agreed on what a koy <em>is</em>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 pb-16 pt-8">
      <!-- ============ Rules ============ -->
      <div class="mb-6 rounded-2xl border border-[#3a2f1e] bg-[#141109] p-5">
        <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] !text-[#c08b3f]">the pen — read before you sort</p>
        <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-[#2e281c] bg-[#0f0d08] p-3">
            <p class="text-xs font-bold !text-[#dfa14e]">🐐🦌 Pen A — domestic sire, wild dam</p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-xs leading-relaxed !text-[#a19aad]"><span dir="rtl" lang="he" class="frank">תַּיִשׁ הַבָּא עַל הַצְּבִיָּיה</span> — a buck goat mates a doe. The father is domestic, the mother is wild (80a:5).</p>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-[#2e281c] bg-[#0f0d08] p-3">
            <p class="text-xs font-bold !text-[#dfa14e]">🦌🐐 Pen B — wild sire, domestic dam</p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-xs leading-relaxed !text-[#a19aad]"><span dir="rtl" lang="he" class="frank">צְבִי הַבָּא עַל הַתְּיָישָׁה</span> — a stag deer mates a nanny goat. The father is wild, the mother is domestic (80a:2, 5).</p>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-[#2e281c] bg-[#0f0d08] p-3 sm:col-span-2">
            <p class="text-xs font-bold !text-[#dfa14e]">🧬 Why the pens differ</p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-xs leading-relaxed !text-[#a19aad]">Both crosses raise the same doubt — <span dir="rtl" lang="he" class="frank">חוֹשְׁשִׁין לְזֶרַע הָאָב</span>, do we worry about the father's line? But <em>which</em> parent supplies the domestic half changes which law even applies, and how far "even a partial sheep" reaches. Rav Pappa maps six real rulings onto these two pens (80a:2–10) — your job is to put each ruling where it belongs.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- ============ Round 1: sort the rulings ============ -->
      <div id="round1"></div>

      <!-- ============ Round 2: whose kid is it ============ -->
      <div id="round2" class="mt-8"></div>

      <!-- ============ Round 3: ten and no more ============ -->
      <div id="round3" class="mt-8"></div>

      <!-- ============ Learn the real daf ============ -->
      <div class="mt-10 rounded-2xl border border-[#2b2438] bg-[#16121d] p-5">
        <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] !text-[#c08b3f]">learn the real daf</p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed !text-[#a19aad]">
          Chullin 80 opens with the koy — deer crossed with goat — and Rav Pappa's careful mapping of
          its laws onto two possible pedigrees. It moves through a real tannaitic dispute over what a
          koy even <em>is</em>, then into forest goats and Rabbi Yitzchak's count of exactly ten kosher
          species in Deuteronomy 14:4–5. The daf closes by turning to the mishna itself, where
          <a class="!text-[#dfa14e] underline hover:!text-[#f2c14e]" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.80a.21">Rabbi Oshaya argues (80a:21)</a>
          that its rulings on slaughtering an animal and its offspring don't follow Rabbi Shimon's view
          that an unfit act of slaughter isn't slaughter at all.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.80a" class="rounded-lg border border-[#c08b3f]/40 bg-[#c08b3f]/10 px-3 py-1.5 text-xs font-bold !text-[#dfa14e] hover:bg-[#c08b3f]/20">Chullin 80 on Sefaria →</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Chullin.80a" class="rounded-lg border border-[#2b2438] px-3 py-1.5 text-xs !text-[#a19aad] hover:!text-[#eae3d2]">Rashi (×24)</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Steinsaltz_on_Chullin.80a" class="rounded-lg border border-[#2b2438] px-3 py-1.5 text-xs !text-[#a19aad] hover:!text-[#eae3d2]">Steinsaltz (×33)</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Rabbeinu_Gershom_on_Chullin.80a" class="rounded-lg border border-[#2b2438] px-3 py-1.5 text-xs !text-[#a19aad] hover:!text-[#eae3d2]">Rabbeinu Gershom (×13)</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_on_Chullin.80a" class="rounded-lg border border-[#2b2438] px-3 py-1.5 text-xs !text-[#a19aad] hover:!text-[#eae3d2]">Tosafot (×12)</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>

  <style>
    .frank {
      font-family: 'Frank Ruhl Libre', 'Times New Roman', serif;
    }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
      .fade-in { animation: fadeIn 0.35s ease both; }
      @keyframes fadeIn { from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(4px); } to { opacity: 1; transform: none; } }
    }
    .chip-pending { cursor: pointer; }
  </style>

  <script>
    const $ = (id) => document.getElementById(id);

    // ================= ROUND 1 — sort the rulings into the right pen =================
    // Every ruling below is Rav Pappa's actual mapping, Chullin 80a:2-10.
    const CHIPS = [
      {
        id: 'blood',
        label: '🩸 Must cover the blood after slaughter (uncertain, so no blessing)',
        pen: 'B',
        why: "Rav Pappa: covering the blood is only ever taught of Pen B — the stag-sired koy. Its wild-side father is why the mishna treats the blood as possibly needing covering at all.",
        ref: 'Chullin 80a:2', refUrl: 'https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.80a.2',
      },
      {
        id: 'gifts',
        label: '🎁 Owed half the priestly gifts (the goat-mother’s half)',
        pen: 'B',
        why: "Rav Pappa: the gifts of the priesthood are likewise only taught of Pen B. Because its mother is the domestic nanny goat, the Rabbis require half the gifts — the domestic half's share.",
        ref: 'Chullin 80a:2, 4', refUrl: 'https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.80a.4',
      },
      {
        id: 'issurA',
        label: '🚫 Rabbanim: forbidden to slaughter it with its young — but not flogged',
        pen: 'A',
        why: 'The Rabbis worry about the father’s line, so this buck-sired koy counts as partly a sheep and the prohibition applies ab initio — but since it is only partly a sheep, the transgression is not definite, so there are no lashes.',
        ref: 'Chullin 80a:6', refUrl: 'https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.80a.6',
      },
      {
        id: 'permitA',
        label: '✅ Rabbi Eliezer: fully permitted — slaughter it and its young the same day',
        pen: 'A',
        why: "Rabbi Eliezer holds we do not say “even a partial sheep” applies the prohibition at all — even granting the paternity concern, this koy never counts as a sheep for this law, so its slaughter with its young is entirely permitted.",
        ref: 'Chullin 80a:7', refUrl: 'https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.80a.7',
      },
      {
        id: 'floggedB',
        label: '🚫⚡ Rabbanim: forbidden — and flogged for it',
        pen: 'B',
        why: 'The Rabbis again invoke “even a partial sheep”: though the stag father makes this koy partly undomesticated, that partial sheep-status is enough to make the transgression definite, so lashes apply.',
        ref: 'Chullin 80a:8', refUrl: 'https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.80a.8',
      },
      {
        id: 'noflogB',
        label: '🚫 Rabbi Eliezer: forbidden — but not flogged',
        pen: 'B',
        why: "Even Rabbi Eliezer agrees there is a prohibition here — worst case, ignoring paternity, the mother alone makes this a plain sheep. But since he rejects “even a partial sheep,” the paternity doubt is enough to block a definite forewarning, so there are no lashes.",
        ref: 'Chullin 80a:9–10', refUrl: 'https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.80a.9',
      },
    ];

    let selected = null;
    const placed = {}; // id -> { pen, correct }

    function chipEl(c) {
      const isPlaced = c.id in placed;
      const cls = isPlaced
        ? (placed[c.id].correct ? 'border-[#9db87a]/60 bg-[#9db87a]/10' : 'border-[#d24a43]/60 bg-[#d24a43]/10')
        : (selected === c.id ? 'border-[#f2c14e] bg-[#f2c14e]/10' : 'border-[#2b2438] bg-[#120f18] chip-pending hover:border-[#8d8798]');
      return `
        <div class="fade-in rounded-xl border p-3 text-xs leading-relaxed !text-[#d8d1c0] ${cls}" data-chip="${c.id}" ${isPlaced ? '' : 'role="button" tabindex="0"'}>
          <p>${c.label}</p>
          ${isPlaced ? `<p class="mt-2 text-[11px] !text-[#a19aad]">${placed[c.id].correct ? '✓ correctly in Pen ' + c.pen : '✗ this one belongs in Pen ' + c.pen}. ${c.why} <a href="${c.refUrl}" class="!text-[#dfa14e] underline hover:!text-[#f2c14e]">${c.ref}</a></p>` : ''}
        </div>`;
    }

    function round1Render() {
      const remaining = CHIPS.filter((c) => !(c.id in placed));
      const done = remaining.length === 0;
      const score = Object.values(placed).filter((p) => p.correct).length;

      $('round1').innerHTML = `
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-[#2b2438] bg-[#16121d] p-5">
          <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] !text-[#c08b3f]">round 1 · sort six rulings into the right pen</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-xs !text-[#a19aad]">Tap a ruling below, then tap the pen you think it belongs to.</p>

          <div class="mt-4 grid gap-2">
            ${remaining.map(chipEl).join('') || '<p class="text-xs italic !text-[#6b6478]">All six rulings sorted.</p>'}
          </div>

          <div class="mt-4 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
            <button id="pen-a" class="rounded-xl border border-[#3a2f1e] bg-[#0f0d08] p-4 text-left hover:border-[#c08b3f] focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-[#f2c14e]" ${selected ? '' : 'disabled'}>
              <p class="text-sm font-bold !text-[#dfa14e]">🐐🦌 Pen A</p>
              <p class="text-[11px] !text-[#a19aad]" dir="rtl" lang="he">תַּיִשׁ הַבָּא עַל הַצְּבִיָּיה</p>
              <div class="mt-2 grid gap-1.5">${CHIPS.filter((c) => c.pen === 'A' && c.id in placed).map(chipEl).join('')}</div>
            </button>
            <button id="pen-b" class="rounded-xl border border-[#3a2f1e] bg-[#0f0d08] p-4 text-left hover:border-[#c08b3f] focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-[#f2c14e]" ${selected ? '' : 'disabled'}>
              <p class="text-sm font-bold !text-[#dfa14e]">🦌🐐 Pen B</p>
              <p class="text-[11px] !text-[#a19aad]" dir="rtl" lang="he">צְבִי הַבָּא עַל הַתְּיָישָׁה</p>
              <div class="mt-2 grid gap-1.5">${CHIPS.filter((c) => c.pen === 'B' && c.id in placed).map(chipEl).join('')}</div>
            </button>
          </div>

          ${done ? `<div class="fade-in mt-4 rounded-xl border border-[#c08b3f]/50 bg-[#c08b3f]/10 p-4 text-center">
            <p class="frank text-lg font-bold !text-[#dfa14e]">${score} / 6 rulings correctly penned</p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-xs !text-[#a19aad]">Same doubt about the father's line, six different outcomes — because which parent is which changes everything.</p>
          </div>` : ''}
        </div>`;

      $('round1').querySelectorAll('[data-chip]').forEach((el) => {
        const id = el.getAttribute('data-chip');
        if (id in placed) return;
        el.addEventListener('click', () => { selected = selected === id ? null : id; round1Render(); });
        el.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => { if (e.key === 'Enter' || e.key === ' ') { e.preventDefault(); selected = selected === id ? null : id; round1Render(); } });
      });
      if (selected) {
        $('pen-a')?.addEventListener('click', () => placeChip('A'));
        $('pen-b')?.addEventListener('click', () => placeChip('B'));
      }
    }

    function placeChip(pen) {
      const c = CHIPS.find((x) => x.id === selected);
      placed[c.id] = { pen: c.pen, correct: pen === c.pen };
      selected = null;
      round1Render();
    }

    round1Render();

    // ================= ROUND 2 — whose kid is it =================
    // The tannaitic/amoraic dispute over what a koy actually is, Chullin 80a:11-12.
    const CLAIMS = [
      {
        id: 'species',
        text: '"A koy is a creature unto itself — the Sages never decided whether it is domestic or wild."',
        he: 'בְּרִיָּה בִּפְנֵי עַצְמָהּ הִיא',
        sages: ['ravyehuda', 'ryosei'],
        ref: 'Chullin 80a:11 (Rav Yehuda) & 80a:12 (Rabbi Yosei)', refUrl: 'https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.80a.11',
      },
      {
        id: 'wildram',
        text: '"The koy is simply the wild ram — nothing more exotic than that."',
        he: 'זֶה אֵיל הַבָּר',
        sages: ['ravnachman', 'tannakamma'],
        ref: 'Chullin 80a:11 (Rav Naḥman) & 80a:12 (first baraita opinion)', refUrl: 'https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.80a.12',
      },
      {
        id: 'hybrid',
        text: '"The koy comes from a goat that mated with a doe."',
        he: 'הַבָּא מִן הַתַּיִישׁ וּמִן הַצְּבִיָּיה',
        sages: ['yeshomrim'],
        ref: 'Chullin 80a:12 ("some say")', refUrl: 'https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.80a.12',
      },
      {
        id: 'domestic',
        text: '"It is a full domestic species — the house of Dushai raised whole flocks of them."',
        he: 'מִין בְּהֵמָה הִיא',
        sages: ['rsbg'],
        ref: 'Chullin 80a:12 (Rabban Shimon ben Gamliel)', refUrl: 'https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.80a.12',
      },
    ];
    const SAGES = [
      { id: 'ravyehuda', label: 'Rav Yehuda' },
      { id: 'ravnachman', label: 'Rav Naḥman' },
      { id: 'tannakamma', label: 'the baraita’s first voice' },
      { id: 'yeshomrim', label: '“others say” (baraita)' },
      { id: 'ryosei', label: 'Rabbi Yosei' },
      { id: 'rsbg', label: 'Rabban Shimon ben Gamliel' },
    ];

    let sageSelected = null;
    const sagePlaced = {}; // sageId -> claimId | 'wrong' marker handled via correctness

    function sageChip(s) {
      const isPlaced = s.id in sagePlaced;
      const cls = isPlaced
        ? 'border-[#9db87a]/60 bg-[#9db87a]/10 !text-[#b9d49a]'
        : (sageSelected === s.id ? 'border-[#f2c14e] bg-[#f2c14e]/10' : 'border-[#2b2438] bg-[#120f18] chip-pending hover:border-[#8d8798]');
      return `<span class="fade-in inline-block rounded-lg border px-3 py-1.5 text-xs font-bold !text-[#d8d1c0] ${cls}" data-sage="${s.id}" ${isPlaced ? '' : 'role="button" tabindex="0"'}>${s.label}</span>`;
    }

    function round2Render() {
      const unplacedSages = SAGES.filter((s) => !(s.id in sagePlaced));
      const done = unplacedSages.length === 0;

      $('round2').innerHTML = `
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-[#2b2438] bg-[#16121d] p-5">
          <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] !text-[#c08b3f]">round 2 · whose kid is it?</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-xs leading-relaxed !text-[#a19aad]">Rav Pappa's rulings all assumed a koy is a hybrid — but the Gemara admits that isn't the only view. Tap a sage below, then tap the claim they actually made.</p>

          <div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-2">${SAGES.map(sageChip).join('')}</div>

          <div class="mt-4 grid gap-3">
            ${CLAIMS.map((cl) => `
              <div id="claim-${cl.id}" class="rounded-xl border border-[#3a2f1e] bg-[#0f0d08] p-3 ${sageSelected ? 'chip-pending hover:border-[#c08b3f]' : ''}" data-claim="${cl.id}" ${sageSelected ? 'role="button" tabindex="0"' : ''}>
                <p class="text-sm !text-[#cfc4a4]">${cl.text}</p>
                <p class="frank mt-1 text-sm !text-[#dfa14e]" dir="rtl" lang="he">${cl.he}</p>
                <div class="mt-2 flex flex-wrap gap-1.5">${cl.sages.filter((sid) => sagePlaced[sid] === cl.id).map((sid) => sageChip(SAGES.find((s) => s.id === sid))).join('')}</div>
                ${cl.sages.every((sid) => sagePlaced[sid] === cl.id) ? `<p class="mt-2 text-[11px] !text-[#8d8798]">Source: <a href="${cl.refUrl}" class="!text-[#dfa14e] underline hover:!text-[#f2c14e]">${cl.ref}</a></p>` : ''}
              </div>`).join('')}
          </div>

          ${done ? `<div class="fade-in mt-4 rounded-xl border border-[#c08b3f]/50 bg-[#c08b3f]/10 p-4 text-center">
            <p class="text-sm !text-[#a19aad]">The Gemara itself says this is <span dir="rtl" lang="he" class="frank">כְּתַנָּאֵי</span> — the amoraic dispute over a koy's identity mirrors an older dispute among the tanna'im. Six sages, three real positions, and no resolution before the daf moves on.</p>
          </div>` : ''}
        </div>`;

      $('round2').querySelectorAll('[data-sage]').forEach((el) => {
        const id = el.getAttribute('data-sage');
        if (id in sagePlaced) return;
        el.addEventListener('click', () => { sageSelected = sageSelected === id ? null : id; round2Render(); });
        el.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => { if (e.key === 'Enter' || e.key === ' ') { e.preventDefault(); sageSelected = sageSelected === id ? null : id; round2Render(); } });
      });
      if (sageSelected) {
        $('round2').querySelectorAll('[data-claim]').forEach((el) => {
          el.addEventListener('click', () => {
            const claimId = el.getAttribute('data-claim');
            sagePlaced[sageSelected] = claimId; // record the guess, right or wrong
            sageSelected = null;
            round2Render();
          });
        });
      }
    }

    round2Render();

    // ================= ROUND 3 — ten and no more =================
    // Forest goats and Rabbi Yitzchak's fixed list of ten kosher species, Chullin 80a:13-17.
    const TEN = {
      domestic: ['שׁוֹר ox', 'שֵׂה כְשָׂבִים sheep', 'שֵׂה עִזִּים goat'],
      wild: ['אַיָּל deer', 'צְבִי gazelle', 'יַחְמוּר fallow deer', 'אַקּוֹ wild goat', 'דִּישֹׁן oryx', 'תְּאוֹ aurochs', 'זָמֶר wild sheep'],
    };
    const VOLLEYS = [
      {
        who: 'Rav Hamnuna', pos: 'opens',
        text: 'Forest goats — wild goats living in the hills — are fit to sacrifice on the altar. They’re not on the wild list, so they must be a kind of domestic goat.',
        ref: 'Chullin 80a:13', refUrl: 'https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.80a.13',
      },
      {
        who: 'Rav Aḥa bar Yaakov', pos: 'objects',
        text: 'Why assume the list is closed? "Deer, gazelle..." are details, then the Torah generalizes to "any wild animal" — a detail-and-generalization reading extends past the ten. Forest goats could just be an unlisted eighth wild species.',
        ref: 'Chullin 80a:14', refUrl: 'https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.80a.14',
      },
      {
        who: 'The Gemara', pos: 'responds',
        text: 'If the generalization reaches past the list anyway, why did the verse bother naming seven details at all? It wouldn’t need to. So: ten kosher species, and no more — forest goats must be domestic.',
        ref: 'Chullin 80a:16', refUrl: 'https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.80a.16',
      },
      {
        who: 'Rav Aḥa, son of Rav Ika', pos: 'objects',
        text: 'Even granting only ten species total — maybe forest goats just are the אַקּוֹ, the wild goat already on the list, not a domestic goat at all.',
        ref: 'Chullin 80a:16', refUrl: 'https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.80a.16',
      },
      {
        who: 'Rav Aḥa, son of Rava', pos: 'objects',
        text: 'Or maybe they’re the תְּאוֹ (aurochs) or the זָמֶר (wild sheep) — also already on the wild list.',
        ref: 'Chullin 80a:17', refUrl: 'https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.80a.17',
      },
      {
        who: 'Rav Ḥanan', pos: 'evidence',
        text: 'Whatever the theory — in practice, Ameimar permits eating the cheilev (forbidden fat) of forest goats. That fat prohibition only lifts for undomesticated game. So in practice, they’re treated as wild.',
        ref: 'Chullin 80a:17', refUrl: 'https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin.80a.17',
      },
    ];

    let volleyIdx = 0;
    let predicted = null;

    function round3Render() {
      const shown = VOLLEYS.slice(0, volleyIdx);
      const finished = volleyIdx >= VOLLEYS.length;

      $('round3').innerHTML = `
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-[#2b2438] bg-[#16121d] p-5">
          <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] !text-[#c08b3f]">round 3 · ten and no more</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-xs leading-relaxed !text-[#a19aad]">
            <span class="frank !text-[#dfa14e]" dir="rtl" lang="he">עֶשֶׂר בְּהֵמוֹת מָנָה הַכָּתוּב, וְתוּ לָא</span> —
            "the verse counted ten kosher animals, and no more" (Rabbi Yitzḥak, Chullin 80a:13), reading Deuteronomy 14:4–5.
          </p>

          <div class="mt-3 grid gap-2 sm:grid-cols-2">
            <div class="rounded-lg border border-[#2e281c] bg-[#0f0d08] p-3">
              <p class="text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wide !text-[#8d8798]">3 domestic</p>
              <p class="mt-1 text-xs !text-[#d8d1c0]">${TEN.domestic.join(' · ')}</p>
            </div>
            <div class="rounded-lg border border-[#2e281c] bg-[#0f0d08] p-3">
              <p class="text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wide !text-[#8d8798]">7 wild</p>
              <p class="mt-1 text-xs !text-[#d8d1c0]">${TEN.wild.join(' · ')}</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-4 rounded-lg border border-[#3a2f1e] bg-[#141109] p-3">
            <p class="text-sm !text-[#eae3d2]">🐐 A forest goat isn't on either list. Where does it belong?</p>
            ${!predicted ? `
              <div class="mt-2 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
                <button id="pred-dom" class="rounded-lg border border-[#2b2438] px-3 py-1.5 text-xs font-bold !text-[#a19aad] hover:!text-[#eae3d2] hover:border-[#8d8798]">A kind of domestic goat</button>
                <button id="pred-wild" class="rounded-lg border border-[#2b2438] px-3 py-1.5 text-xs font-bold !text-[#a19aad] hover:!text-[#eae3d2] hover:border-[#8d8798]">An unlisted wild species</button>
              </div>` : `<p class="mt-2 text-xs italic !text-[#8d8798]">You guessed: ${predicted === 'dom' ? 'a kind of domestic goat' : 'an unlisted wild species'}. Watch the sages argue it out below — six real volleys, in order.</p>`}
          </div>

          ${predicted ? `
          <div class="mt-4 grid gap-2">
            ${shown.map((v) => `
              <div class="fade-in rounded-xl border border-[#2b2438] bg-[#120f18] p-3">
                <p class="text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] !text-[#8d8798]">${v.who} · ${v.pos}</p>
                <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed !text-[#d8d1c0]">${v.text}</p>
                <p class="mt-1 text-[11px] !text-[#6b6478]">Source: <a href="${v.refUrl}" class="!text-[#dfa14e] underline hover:!text-[#f2c14e]">${v.ref}</a></p>
              </div>`).join('')}
          </div>
          ${!finished ? `<button id="next-volley" class="mt-3 w-full rounded-xl border border-[#c08b3f]/50 bg-[#c08b3f]/15 px-4 py-3 text-sm font-bold !text-[#dfa14e] hover:bg-[#c08b3f]/25 focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-[#f2c14e]">${volleyIdx === 0 ? 'Hear the first volley →' : 'Next volley →'}</button>` : `
          <div class="fade-in mt-3 rounded-xl border border-[#c08b3f]/50 bg-[#c08b3f]/10 p-4 text-center">
            <p class="text-sm !text-[#a19aad]">The Gemara never picks a winner. Forest goats stay an open question — the daf just tells you the one practical fact it has: Ameimar treats their fat as wild-game fat, permitted where a domestic animal's would not be.</p>
          </div>`}` : ''}
        </div>`;

      $('pred-dom')?.addEventListener('click', () => { predicted = 'dom'; round3Render(); });
      $('pred-wild')?.addEventListener('click', () => { predicted = 'wild'; round3Render(); });
      $('next-volley')?.addEventListener('click', () => { volleyIdx++; round3Render(); });
    }

    round3Render();
  </script>
</Layout>
